  "name": "true_sphenoidal",
  "description": "True sphenoidal montage: a double-banana variant that threads the surgically placed sphenoidal electrodes Sp1 and Sp2 into the anterior temporal chains so mesial-temporal activity is visible. 'True' distinguishes this from anterior-temporal proxy montages that use surface positions like FT9/FT10 in place of real sphenoidal leads. Each temporal chain becomes 5 channels (Fp1-F7, F7-Sp1, Sp1-T3, T3-T5, T5-O1 and mirror). Sphenoidal pairs (F7-Sp1, Sp1-T3 and F8-Sp2, Sp2-T4) are tinted distinctly. Spacers fall at the left/right transitions around the midline. Requires Sp1 and Sp2 in rec_labels.",
